# Theme token sync (critical)

Hex palettes live in **two places**. Changing one without the other is a bug.

| JS (`src/tokens.ts`) | CSS (`src/styles.css`) |
| --- | --- |
| `AV` | `[data-av-theme='phosphor']` / `.av-theme` default |
| `AV_EDITORIAL` | `[data-av-theme='editorial']` (light) |
| `AV_EDITORIAL_DARK` | editorial `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` |

## Required workflow

1. Edit the CSS `--av-*` assignment **and** the matching JS map in the same change.
2. Match keys: `surface2` ↔ `--av-surface-2`, `signalHot` ↔ `--av-signal-hot`, `phosphorBright` ↔ `--av-phosphor-bright`, `onPrimary` ↔ `--av-on-primary`, `accentSoft` ↔ `--av-accent-soft`.
3. Prefer `#RRGGBB` uppercase in JS; CSS may be lowercase — same digits.
4. If CSS uses `color-mix(...)` for hairline/border, keep a solid stand-in hex in JS and leave a one-line comment.
5. Update `AV_RGB` when phosphor `AV` RGB-consuming colors change (canvas/LED).
6. Export new maps from `src/index.ts` when adding them.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — CSS-only accent tweak
// styles.css: --av-signal: #9b1c1c;  (tokens.ts left at old value)

// ✅ GOOD — both updated together
// styles.css + tokens.ts AV_EDITORIAL.signal = '#9B1C1C'
```
